the watchdog starts
!panic: a signal handler jumped out of the code it interrupted while that code was inside this runtime's allocator, which nothing will ever finish: what runs after such a jump is undefined, the allocator's lock and lists may be left half written, so the program stops here, before the jump. A handler that ends work by jumping (`siglongjmp`, `longjmp`) may leave only code it is safe to abandon, and this runtime's allocation is not: count the signal instead, with `hero_signal_watch(sig: i32) -> i64` and `hero_signal_take(sig: i32) -> i64` (`hero_os.h`), and let the function return
